# The Treaty Grid and Scores of a twelve-empire game (GitHub issue #3), in the original's large
# dialog (780x475, spec 06 §1): ten empires a page, each column headed by the empire's flag over
# the first letters of its name; every name, treaty code and figure fits its place and is drawn
# whole, without "…" (assert-fits, assert-whole), on both pages (docs/BUILDING.md "Input
# scripts"). v0.9.0 squeezed the last columns of the grid and cut the scores' figures.
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --quick-start --empires=12 --systems=16 --seed=3 --turns=40 --open=none --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-screen game
repeat 20
  click item:"*(suggested)" optional timeout=5
end
key F9
wait-window empires
click item:"Treaty Grid" in=empires
wait-window treaty-grid
assert-present item:"Empires 11-12" in=treaty-grid
assert-fits treaty-grid
assert-whole treaty-grid
screenshot treaty-grid.png
click item:"Empires 11-12" in=treaty-grid
wait 2
assert-fits treaty-grid
assert-whole treaty-grid
key Escape
wait-closed treaty-grid
click item:Scores in=empires
wait-window scores
assert-fits scores
assert-whole scores
screenshot scores.png
click item:"Empires 11-12" in=scores
wait 2
assert-fits scores
assert-whole scores
key Escape
wait-closed scores
key Escape
wait-closed empires
